:["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:aa78c9a77de122c492ca","f":"How many marks is the Shakespeare essay worth, including accuracy?","b":"25","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:9d954255145b73444cb2","f":"How many marks is the anthology comparison worth?","b":"25","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:c8d7e9df02e769fdabdf","f":"How many marks is the single unseen poem response worth?","b":"15","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:7a181b34d1242f67a318","f":"How many marks is the unseen poetry comparison worth?","b":"25","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:945b334a7d055d4ebd3a","f":"How many marks does the A Christmas Carol question carry?","b":"40","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:c5492c6aa4cdb7b6c333","f":"How does Shakespeare present Macbeth’s ambition in the play as a whole?","b":"Model: Macbeth’s desire for power leads him to murder Duncan. Marking points: support a developed interpretation and analyse Shakespeare’s methods. Trap: retelling the plot.","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:79923abfa0121b35364f","f":"How does the writer present responsibility in An Inspector Calls?","b":"Model: Sheila accepts responsibility for her treatment of Eva. Marking points: use the extract and whole play; analyse dramatic methods. Trap: ignoring the extract.","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:4c85c2b4ab01ffcc763b","f":"How does Dickens present Scrooge’s transformation in A Christmas Carol?","b":"Model: Scrooge’s generosity at the end reverses his earlier selfishness. Marking points: support a reading across the novel and analyse methods in context. Trap: recounting events alone.","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:ab043606c2bd4439640d","f":"How does Blake present education in The Schoolboy?","b":"Model: Blake contrasts the child’s pleasure outdoors with the misery he associates with school. Marking points: support an interpretation with textual detail and analyse language or structure. Trap: retell the poem without explaining effects.","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:cd8e8cb8a9c2163e374a","f":"Compare experiences of war in Disabled and Drummer Hodge.","b":"Model: Owen depicts a veteran’s continuing isolation, while Hardy presents a young soldier buried far from home. Marking points: analyse methods in both poems, compare interpretations and relate relevant context. Trap: discuss only one poem.","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:95e7f848d88794791ae6","f":"How does Shakespeare use Lady Macbeth’s sleepwalking to present guilt?","b":"Model: Her attempt to clean an imagined stain suggests that the murder continues to trouble her. Marking points: support a focused interpretation and analyse dramatic methods. Trap: describe the murder without analysing the scene.","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:ef2196da369bd146e67f","f":"Which assessment objectives does the Eduqas anthology section assess?","b":"AO1, AO2 and AO3","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:b3d69a6babcbd1a91648","f":"Which assessment objectives does the unseen poetry section assess?","b":"AO1 and AO2","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:91ef317745a851f26970","f":"Which assessment objectives does the Shakespeare section assess?","b":"AO1, AO2 and AO4","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:2d99026e24d862099649","f":"Which assessment objectives does the 19th-century prose section assess?","b":"AO1, AO2 and AO3","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:eb3cd4bda236082c8b8a","f":"In the anthology comparison, which poem does the student select?","b":"The second anthology poem","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:31d41308ac64cb0d2eef","f":"How many marks are allocated to the first anthology poem response?","b":"15","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:2b468ed87ce149618d75","f":"How many marks are allocated to the post-1914 drama question?","b":"40","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-englit-C720QS-mark:1e7ef7548624c01bbc62","f":"Compare how The Schoolboy and I Wandered Lonely as a Cloud present nature.","b":"Model: Blake contrasts natural freedom with school, while Wordsworth shows remembered flowers restoring pleasure. Marking points: compare supported interpretations and analyse each poet’s methods and relevant context. Trap: write separate summaries without comparison.","t":["PPP::Eduqas::C720QS","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"Eduqas GCSE English Literature C720QS – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"}]$j$::jsonb) as x(k text,f text,b text,t text[],p text) join public.flashcard_catalogue_items i on i.catalogue_id='EDUQAS_GCSE_ENGLIT_C720QS_MARK' and i.stable_key=x.k on conflict (version_id,catalogue_card_id) do nothing;
